Brown Butter Cinnamon Swirl Banana Bread
  --Rosana Machiela

Bread:
10 tbsp butter, cut into pieces
3-4 ripe bananas, plus 1 for topping (optional)
2 tsp vanilla
3 eggs
2 c ap flour
1/2 c  sugar
1/2 c light brown sugar
1 ½ tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp baking soda
1 tsp salt
2 tsp cinnamon

Preheat the oven to 350F. Grease a 9x5" loaf pan and set aside. In a small saucepan, over medium low heat, melt butter and cook until it becomes a light amber color and has a nutty aroma. Remove from heat and transfer to a bowl to keep it from cooking further. Allow to cool. In a large bowl, mash bananas using a fork. Whisk in the cooled butter, eggs and vanilla. In a separate bowl, combine the flour, brown sugar, sugar, baking powder, baking soda, salt and cinnamon. Whisk to combine. Fold the dry mixture into the wet mixture until just combined. 

Swirl:
3 tbsp butter, melted
5 tbsp brown sugar
4 tbsp granulated sugar
3 tbsp cinnamon

Combine swirl ingredients in a bowl. Spread half the batter evenly into prepared pan. Dollop the cinnamon mixture over the batter and make swirls using a knife or skewer. Pour the remaining batter over the top.

Topping (optional):
1 banana, sliced in half lengthwise
Toasted walnuts, sunflower seeds, bee pollen, sesame seeds, honey

Top with additional banana, cut in half lengthwise. Bake for 45-50 min or until a knife inserted in the center comes out clean. Allow to cool for 10 min before transferring to a cooling rack. After banana bread has cooled, top with toasted and chopped nuts and seeds.

